// Radio budget (playtest row 6, "the dispatcher and cops are way too talkative"): a 5-minute
// city chase at 23:00 on the full 12×12 city. The racer roams at twice the limit, so it is
// spotted, chased, and escapes or gets caught several times. Radio lines per minute of sim time
// while some racer is in a pursuit must stay at or under 10 (rates are pooled over runs).
// The calm budget (<= 4 lines/min with nobody wanted) is radio_calm_patrol.ron's: since round 12c
// a pursuit here starts within ~11 s, so each run has only a few calm seconds and one call line
// ("caller reports reckless driver") made the calm rate 4.5/min over ~45 s pooled.
(
    name: "police_radio_city_chase",
    seed: 600,
    city: (nx: 12, ny: 12, seed: 1),
    time_of_day_h: 23.0,
    duration_s: 300.0,
    runs: 4,
    racers: [(district: Core, speed_factor: 2.5)],
    expect: [
        (metric: "pursuits", min: 1, max: 1000),
        (metric: "radio_per_min_pursuit", min: 0.5, max: 10.0),
    ],
)
